  <slot slot="title">Dividend ETF History</slot>
  <slot slot="subtitle">Distribution records, payment schedules, yield definitions, and the mechanics that turn option premiums and dividend streams into monthly checks.</slot>

  <p>An exchange-traded fund's "dividend history" is more than a list of past payments — it encodes how the fund actually generates income. A traditional dividend-growth ETF like SCHD returns shareholder cash from the underlying companies' earnings. A covered-call ETF like JEPI or SPYI returns cash from selling index options on top of the underlying dividends. A single-stock option-income ETF like ULTY or MSTY returns cash mostly from selling calls on one volatile name — and most of that cash is return of capital. The reported <em>yield</em> you see on a financial site depends entirely on which of these mechanisms the fund uses, which is why two funds with the same "12% yield" can have wildly different total returns.</p>

  <p>This hub collects every dividend-ETF distribution record we maintain. Each article documents payment dates, distribution amounts, the fund's mechanics, the difference between distribution rate and SEC yield, and the total-return context. Use the sub-topic groups below to navigate by family, and the comparison tables to spot the structural differences between funds that look similar on the surface.</p>

  <h2>Reading path by experience</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Beginner</strong> — start with <a href="/articles/what-are-dividends/">What Are Dividends?</a> and <a href="/articles/dividend-yield/">Dividend Yield Explained</a>, then read the SCHD dividend history as the simplest example of a traditional dividend-growth ETF.</li>
    <li><strong>Intermediate</strong> — read <a href="/articles/jepi-dividend/">JEPI Dividend</a> and <a href="/articles/qqqi-dividend/">QQQI Dividend</a> to understand the covered-call income model, then compare the distribution rates on the table below.</li>
    <li><strong>Advanced</strong> — read the YieldMax and single-stock option-income articles (<a href="/articles/ulty-dividend/">ULTY</a>, <a href="/articles/msty-dividend-income/">MSTY</a>, <a href="/articles/bito-dividend/">BITO</a>) and the <a href="/articles/dividend-calculator-guide/">Dividend Calculator Guide</a> to model after-tax income across these structures.</li>
  </ul>

